# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages header rules.
#
# Vercel ignores this file and reads vercel.json instead, so on the current
# deploy target it is inert. It is kept and corrected rather than deleted
# because it is a live landmine: it previously sent a robots header on /*
# that told crawlers not to index, follow, archive, or snippet ANY page.
# That would deindex the entire site the moment it was deployed to a host
# honouring this format. The old comment claimed it was for preview URLs,
# but the rule was not scoped to previews in any way.
#
# Preview deployments should be excluded from indexing by the host's own
# preview-protection setting (Vercel: Deployment Protection), not by a
# blanket header that also ships to production.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
